  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f^{\\prime}(1)=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}$; As function is differentiable so it is continuous as it is given that $\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(1+h)}{h}=5$ and hence $f(1)=0$\nHence $f^{\\prime}(1)=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(1+h)}{h}=5$\nHence (C) is the correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
